{"text": " I didn't tell my girlfriend that her pet had died. She only found out when she got back from her trip. His name was Gus. He was a pet snake she'd had since she was 8. Yeah, a snake. Maybe not everyone's idea of a pet, but to her, he was family. Gus was getting old. We knew he didn't have much time left, but when he finally died, I still broke down crying. And my girlfriend was in another country, visiting her brother for his birthday. Things with her family had been complicated for a long time. They'd only just started getting better. She really wanted to reconnect with them, and this trip meant a lot to her. So now, I had to make a decision. Call her and tell her Gus was gone? I knew she'd be devastated, and it could ruin her whole trip. Or let her spend a few days with her family, then tell her face to face? I went with the second option. When she flew home, I picked her up at the airport and told her everything. Gus had died, and I deliberately kept it from her while she was away. She didn't say a word the entire drive home. At home, we put Gus in a box we'd kept for this moment and buried him together. Then she finally said, I still love you, but I don't like you right now. I understood why she was angry, so I didn't argue. Later, I made dinner, and we both ended up crying at the table. Before bed, I asked if I should sleep on the couch. She said I'd be a dead man if I slept anywhere other than our bed. No, we didn't break up. We're still together, and we both still miss Gus. I don't regret waiting until she came home. But I understand why she was upset with me.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 2.38, "text": " I didn't tell my girlfriend that her pet had died.", "tokens": [50364, 286, 994, 380, 980, 452, 10369, 300, 720, 3817, 632, 4539, 13, 50516], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1367152622767857, "compression_ratio": 1.6578073089700998, "no_speech_prob": 0.011530263349413872, "words": [{"word": " I", "start": 0.0, "end"